The Mathews girls junior varsity volleyball team defeated King and Queen Wednesday to clinch the Tidewater District regular-season title. The Blue Devils were forced to three games. They won the first 15-3, lost the second 11-15, then rolled 15-1 in the finale.
''In the second game we just didn't serve well,'' said Mathews coach Pat Moughon. ''But we had good teamwork the whole match and things started clicking in the third game.''
The victory gave Mathews a 6-2 record in the district and 12-4 overall. The Blue Devils will host West Point, the No. 2 team in the district, for the tournament title at 6 p.m. Thursday. The Blue Devils are 2-0 against West Point this season, including an exciting 15-11, 9-15, 15-12 victory Feb. 6.
Against King and Queen, the Blue Devils scored seven points on Marie Callis' serves in the first game and seven on Juanita Romero's serves in the third game. Moughon also cited the solid play of Lindsay Thomas, Jackie Keenan, Tina Carmine and Samantha Hardesty.
